extends ../../../../../designs/mockup-kit/page.pug

include ../mixins/backup.pug

block title
  | icloud-backup — backup · UI mockups

//-
  The page a signed-in person sees from then on. One dispatcher draws every
  state; copy and sample data are in src/data/backup.mjs.

block page
  +mockPage('max-w-[1760px]')(class='page')
    +mockHead({ eyebrow: 'icloud-backup · /', title: 'Backup', back: true })
      p What a signed-in person sees from then on, one screen per state of their backup. Each has a status badge, one headline, and at most one accent button: #[+code('Open my photos')], #[+code('Sign in again')] or #[+code('Try again')]. Only a live backup wears the pulsing dot. Each state is a frame showing 1280 and 390 side by side.

    - const c = { queued, preparing, downloading, reconnecting, finishing, done, reauth, paused, failed }
    each s, i in states
      +mockFrame(s.key, s.label, { num: String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0'), caption: s.caption })
        div(class='flex flex-wrap items-start gap-x-8 gap-y-6')
          div(class='flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3')
            +backupScreen('desktop', s, c)
            +frameLabel Desktop · 1280
          div(class='flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3')
            +backupScreen('mobile', s, c)
            +frameLabel Mobile · 390
